x86_64-linux  Seven names cxx1 emits and clang does not, and none that differ: _ZTV2PW, _ZTI2PW, _ZTS2PW and the type_info of its two empty bases, _ZTI2E1/_ZTS2E1 and _ZTI2E2/_ZTS2E2. PW is polymorphic through PV and adds no virtual of its own, so it has no key function; clang emits such a vtable only in a translation unit that constructs a PW, and this one never does - the case only measures where PW's bases lie. cxx1 emits every polymorphic class's vtable where the class is defined, and the vtable's RTTI names the bases, which is where the two empties' type_info come from. Every name for the 45 non-polymorphic classes agrees.
arm64-darwin  The same seven, with the leading underscore.
x86_64-windows  Seven cxx1-only names again, none differing: the vftables ??_7PV@@6B@ and ??_7PW@@6B@ and PV's five RTTI objects (??_R0 to ??_R4). The Microsoft ABI has no key function - a vftable is emitted, COMDAT, by every translation unit that constructs the class - and nothing here constructs a PV or a PW, so clang emits none. cxx1 emits them where the class is defined.
